## else if
What if you have more than two options? Chain conditions with `else if`:

```rust
let x: i32 = 15;
if x > 20 {
    println!("High");
} else if x > 10 {
    println!("Medium");
} else {
    println!("Low");
}
// prints: Medium
```

Rust checks each condition top to bottom. The first one that's true runs, and the rest are skipped. `else` at the end catches everything that didn't match.

You can chain as many `else if` blocks as you want.

